{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} .*D(186|191|198|207|265|368|69[1-9]|70[0-9]|71[01]|720|721)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n 'round 4[45]|number answers|D72[012]' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; rg -n 'CREATE TABLE.*(judgements|views|rungs|evidence|dependencies|model_calls)' src\"","aggregated_output":"2476:## D186 · 2026-10-26 · Asset-thesis rungs describe business outcomes; the favourable end is registered per thesis\n2503:## D191 · 2026-10-26 · Theme theses reach every company; no named dependant is required to open one\n2559:## D198 · 2026-10-27 · A judgement reads the evidence in view, not everything in force\n2631:## D207 · 2026-10-28 · Statements are filed by a separate placement call under the one-home rule; an unfiled statement is kept (extraction v20, `poc-v36`)\n3005:## D254 · 2026-11-01 · Placement: a question's code-written 'takes' line is the one rule for its file; D207's \"company-wide figure questions take only their own figures\" is retired\n3084:## D265 · 2026-11-02 · Extraction v72 / poc-v92 is the version: the default configuration, the base every later change builds on, the control of every later measurement; D207's narrowest rule is enforced in code\n3960:## D368 · 2026-11-05 · Alex's answers to the seven items left open by the consolidation\n4345:## D398 · 2026-11-10 · The clean ladder step carries D186: ranges against the reference, the favourable end registered, labels by code\n5428:## D480 · 2026-11-13 · Under choice 3, production's opening rule is probed with a price (D191 point 4, D368 item 1) on its stored requests (council consensus under D439)\n6353:## D532 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the two filing decisions stand as traced, a common mechanism is not established; next a bounded $0 trace of the dependency lead under D368's direction (council consensus, reflection round 23)\n6375:## D533 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: this stretch of the lean investigation is closed and consolidated; the default and both systems stay; next a separate $0 assessment of D368's dependency channel on a stored, correctly directed case (council consensus, reflection round 24)\n6411:## D535 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the one-chain ordering proof of D368's direction is accepted with its limits; a source-backed case and a verified pre-judgement state of 2026-07-14 come before any measurement design (council consensus, reflection round 26)\n10212:## D685 · 2026-11-20 · Under D684 (councils I–K): the fresh test cannot be fed; H1 fails its diagnostic; the judge line pauses within D198; phase 2 (opening) starts\n10375:## D691 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A after council Q: no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents\n10398:## D692 · 2026-11-20 · Under Alex's A (D691): the dependency probe passes its registered rule; the dependency design review reopens at $0\n10414:## D693 · 2026-11-21 · Under Alex's A (D691): the design for linking related questions reaches council consensus at $0; three choices go to Alex before any build or send; the self-made reference is traced\n10439:## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10454:## D695 · 2026-11-21 · Alex narrows the first linking version to number questions, one of them newly opened\n10467:## D696 · 2026-11-21 · Alex keeps the July test's $0.15 limit as a reservation stop priced from each request's size\n10482:## D697 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the $0 proof of the linking version; the July comparison is sent (D694 (c), D696)\n10493:## D698 · 2026-11-21 · The July test of the linking version passes its frozen rule; next steps go to Alex\n10505:## D699 · 2026-11-21 · Alex continues with A: the whole-window measurement of the linking version, designed with the council at $0 first\n10515:## D700 · 2026-11-21 · Alex approves a $0.10 ceiling for the census of the link decisions before the whole-window run\n10525:## D701 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the census harness (rounds 13–16); the census of link decisions is sent under D700\n10541:## D702 · 2026-11-21 · The census of link decisions passes its registered gate; council R: probe a sharpened link question before buying judgements\n10556:## D703 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses to probe a sharpened link question before the paid run\n10567:## D704 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the version-2 link question for its probe (rounds 18–19); the probe is sent under D703\n10583:## D705 · 2026-11-21 · The version-2 link question passes its registered gate; council R: version 2 goes to the paid design\n10594:## D706 · 2026-11-21 · poc-v120 (link questions version 2) passes council review as a product configuration; the paid design needs four changes\n10611:## D707 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the paid design (version 6, rounds 22–27) for building its harness\n10625:## D708 · 2026-11-21 · Council R (reflection, round 31): a one-pair pilot before the full paid comparison\n10641:## D709 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the pilot of the paid comparison (rounds 32–36); the send waits for Alex's ceiling\n10652:## D710 · 2026-11-21 · Alex approves a $2.50 ceiling for the pilot; pair 1 is sent\n10660:## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\n10839:## D720 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens the double-count design; the diagnosis finds the class in the frozen product too\n10859:## D721 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 43/43b: the double-count premise is partly falsified by the frozen gold; recommend closing the design with nothing to build; D711's H4 reading corrected\n449:- Alex closed the double-count design with nothing changed (D722, 2026-11-22; his words are in the decision log). poc-v118 stays\n451:- Why (D721): the frozen gold's q01 lists the Vera CPU target among the drivers above consensus, so the diagnosis's premise was\n452:  not the ruler's. D711's H4 is corrected to four unsupported increments. D721's findings are recorded, not worked on.\n492:  An analyst would use it for sources and milestones, not for its number answers: linked number questions contradict each other in\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\nD=decimal.Decimal\ndef db(i,name='\\\\''views'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\nv=db(2);a=db(2,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\nfor c in (v,a):\n for r in c.execute(\\\"select name,sql from sqlite_master where type='\\\\''table'\\\\''\\\"):\n  print(r['\\\\''name'\\\\''], '\\\\'' '\\\\''.join((r['\\\\''sql'\\\\''] or '\\\\'''\\\\'').split()))\nfor x in v.execute(\\\"select view_id,question,kind from views where view_id in ('\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v29'\\\\'')\\\"):\n print(dict(x))\nfor j in v.execute(\\\"select * from judgements where view_id in ('\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v29'\\\\'') and publication_day='\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\''\\\"):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\'']); print(j['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],d.keys(),[(k,str(val)[:260]) for k,val in d.items()]); break'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\nD=decimal.Decimal\ndef db(i,name='\\\\''views'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\nv=db(2);a=db(2,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\nfor c in (v,a):\n for r in c.execute(\\\"select name,sql from sqlite_master where type='\\\\''table'\\\\''\\\"):\n  print(r['\\\\''name'\\\\''], '\\\\'' '\\\\''.join((r['\\\\''sql'\\\\''] or '\\\\'''\\\\'').split()))\nfor x in v.execute(\\\"select view_id,question,kind from views where view_id in ('\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v29'\\\\'')\\\"):\n print(dict(x))\nfor j in v.execute(\\\"select * from judgements where view_id in ('\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v29'\\\\'') and publication_day='\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\''\\\"):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\'']); print(j['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],d.keys(),[(k,str(val)[:260]) for k,val in d.items()]); break'\"","aggregated_output":"views CREATE TABLE views (view_id text primary key, object_id text, object_kind text, kind text, looks_at text, question text, due_day text, year text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text, created_at text)\nrungs CREATE TABLE rungs (view_id text, position integer, label text, condition text, lo real, hi real)\nview_keys CREATE TABLE view_keys (view_id text primary key, measure text, scope text, scope_key text, period_start text, period_end text, basis text, unit text, event_type text, seq integer, scope_source text, key_version integer)\nview_switches CREATE TABLE view_switches (id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, open integer, reason text, by_whom text, after_seq integer)\nsqlite_sequence CREATE TABLE sqlite_sequence(name,seq)\njudgements CREATE TABLE judgements (judgement_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, rung integer, reasons text, cited_evidence_json text, cited_views_json text, pushes_json text, changed integer, why_changed text, config_checksum text, call_id integer, request_sha256 text, publication_day text, theme_pushes_json text, reference text, implied_outcome text)\nevidence CREATE TABLE evidence (evidence_id text primary key, quote text, one_line text, speaker text, original_who text, original_day text, tier text, event_time text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text)\nevidence_sources CREATE TABLE evidence_sources (id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, input_id text, category text, publication_day text, location text, seq integer)\nevidence_links CREATE TABLE evidence_links (id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, view_id text, seq integer)\nreplacements CREATE TABLE replacements (id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer)\nrevisions CREATE TABLE revisions (id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer)\nsame_claims CREATE TABLE same_claims (id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, seq integer)\ndependencies CREATE TABLE dependencies (dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer)\ndependency_resolutions CREATE TABLE dependency_resolutions (id integer primary key autoincrement, dependency_id integer, resolved_to text, reason text, seq integer)\nsuccessions CREATE TABLE successions (id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, succeeds text, seq integer)\nhandovers CREATE TABLE handovers (id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, seq integer, handover_json text)\nmatch_records CREATE TABLE match_records (id integer primary key autoincrement, seq integer, input_id text, call_no integer, shown_json text, request_sha256 text, call_id integer, decisions_json text, checks_json text, written_json text)\nprocessing_steps CREATE TABLE processing_steps (id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, sequence_no integer, step text, result text, reason text, publication_day text, at text)\nreview_pool_entries CREATE TABLE review_pool_entries (id integer primary key autoincrement, kind text, key text, example_json text, seq integer)\nlate_statements CREATE TABLE late_statements (id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, evidence_quote text, reason text, seq integer)\ndays_completed CREATE TABLE days_completed (id integer primary key autoincrement, day text, seq integer, at text)\nthesis_groups CREATE TABLE thesis_groups (group_id text primary key, name text, scope text, aliases text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text)\nthesis_group_members CREATE TABLE thesis_group_members (id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, basis text)\nthesis_group_aliases CREATE TABLE thesis_group_aliases (id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, alias text, seq integer, input_id text)\ngroups_fts CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE groups_fts using fts5(group_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\ngroups_fts_data CREATE TABLE 'groups_fts_data'(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, block BLOB)\ngroups_fts_idx CREATE TABLE 'groups_fts_idx'(segid, term, pgno, PRIMARY KEY(segid, term)) WITHOUT ROWID\ngroups_fts_content CREATE TABLE 'groups_fts_content'(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, c0, c1)\ngroups_fts_docsize CREATE TABLE 'groups_fts_docsize'(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, sz BLOB)\ngroups_fts_config CREATE TABLE 'groups_fts_config'(k PRIMARY KEY, v) WITHOUT ROWID\nviews_fts CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE views_fts using fts5(view_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\nviews_fts_data CREATE TABLE 'views_fts_data'(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, block BLOB)\nviews_fts_idx CREATE TABLE 'views_fts_idx'(segid, term, pgno, PRIMARY KEY(segid, term)) WITHOUT ROWID\nviews_fts_content CREATE TABLE 'views_fts_content'(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, c0, c1)\nviews_fts_docsize CREATE TABLE 'views_fts_docsize'(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, sz BLOB)\nviews_fts_config CREATE TABLE 'views_fts_config'(k PRIMARY KEY, v) WITHOUT ROWID\nmodel_calls CREATE TABLE model_calls ( call_id integer primary key autoincrement, purpose text, config_version text, config_checksum text, model text, request_sha256 text unique, request_json text, response_json text, answer_json text, prompt_chars integer, input_tokens integer, output_tokens integer, cost_usd real, seconds real, created_at text )\nsqlite_sequence CREATE TABLE sqlite_sequence(name,seq)\n{'view_id': 'v14', 'question': 'How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'kind': 'asset'}\n{'view_id': 'v16', 'question': 'How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?', 'kind': 'asset'}\n{'view_id': 'v29', 'question': \"How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\", 'kind': 'asset'}\n{'view_id': 'v6', 'question': 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?', 'kind': 'theme'}\n{'view_id': 'v9', 'question': 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'kind': 'asset'}\nv14 8729 dict_keys(['max_completion_tokens', 'messages', 'model', 'reasoning_effort', 'response_format']) [('max_completion_tokens', '16000'), ('messages', \"[{'content': 'You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis\\\\'s current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not \"), ('model', 'gpt-6-luna'), ('reasoning_effort', 'medium'), ('response_format', \"{'json_schema': {'name': 'judgement', 'schema': {'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'cites': {'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'type': 'array'}, 'cites_views': {'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'type': 'array'}, 'implied_outc\")]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\nD=decimal.Decimal\ndef db(i,name='\\\\''views'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef req(a,j):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n assert c and c['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\'']==j['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''] and c['\\\\''purpose'\\\\'']=='\\\\''judgement'\\\\'',dict(j)\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\''])\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\''\"'^- (e'\"\\\\d+) \\\\[.*?(?=\"'^- e'\"\\\\d+ \\\\[|\\\\Z)'\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\ndef evidence(t):\n b=t.split('\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0]\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\n return m\ndef user(d):\n return next(m['\\\\''content'\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\''messages'\\\\''] if m['\\\\''role'\\\\'']=='\\\\''user'\\\\'')\nfor i,ids,day in [(2,['\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v29'\\\\''],'\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\''),(3,['\\\\''v3'\\\\'','\\\\''v41'\\\\''],'\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\'')]:\n v=db(i); a=db(i,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\n for id in ids:\n  j=v.execute('\\\\''select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1'\\\\'',(id,day)).fetchone()\n  if not j: print('\\\\''missing'\\\\'',i,id);continue\n  d,raw=req(a,j); t=user(d); e=evidence(t)\n  print('\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'',i,id,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''seq'\\\\''],t.split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n[Evidence'\\\\'')[0], '\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'',len(e), re.findall(r'\\\\''\\\\[Not shown:.*?\\\\]'\\\\'',t), '\\\\''themes'\\\\'',re.findall(r'\\\\''\\\\[Themes in force, \\\\d+\\\\]'\\\\'',t))\n  print('\\\\''RAW'\\\\'', {k:x for k,x in raw.items() if k not in ('\\\\''pushes'\\\\'','\\\\''theme_pushes'\\\\'')})\n  for k in json.loads(j['\\\\''cited_evidence_json'\\\\'']): print(e[k])\n  print(t[t.index('\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\''):].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\nAnswer'\\\\'')[0])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\nD=decimal.Decimal\ndef db(i,name='\\\\''views'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef req(a,j):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n assert c and c['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\'']==j['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''] and c['\\\\''purpose'\\\\'']=='\\\\''judgement'\\\\'',dict(j)\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\''])\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\''\"'^- (e'\"\\\\d+) \\\\[.*?(?=\"'^- e'\"\\\\d+ \\\\[|\\\\Z)'\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\ndef evidence(t):\n b=t.split('\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0]\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\n return m\ndef user(d):\n return next(m['\\\\''content'\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\''messages'\\\\''] if m['\\\\''role'\\\\'']=='\\\\''user'\\\\'')\nfor i,ids,day in [(2,['\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v29'\\\\''],'\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\''),(3,['\\\\''v3'\\\\'','\\\\''v41'\\\\''],'\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\'')]:\n v=db(i); a=db(i,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\n for id in ids:\n  j=v.execute('\\\\''select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1'\\\\'',(id,day)).fetchone()\n  if not j: print('\\\\''missing'\\\\'',i,id);continue\n  d,raw=req(a,j); t=user(d); e=evidence(t)\n  print('\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'',i,id,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''seq'\\\\''],t.split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n[Evidence'\\\\'')[0], '\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'',len(e), re.findall(r'\\\\''\\\\[Not shown:.*?\\\\]'\\\\'',t), '\\\\''themes'\\\\'',re.findall(r'\\\\''\\\\[Themes in force, \\\\d+\\\\]'\\\\'',t))\n  print('\\\\''RAW'\\\\'', {k:x for k,x in raw.items() if k not in ('\\\\''pushes'\\\\'','\\\\''theme_pushes'\\\\'')})\n  for k in json.loads(j['\\\\''cited_evidence_json'\\\\'']): print(e[k])\n  print(t[t.index('\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\''):].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\nAnswer'\\\\'')[0])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 25, in <module>\n  File \"<string>\", line 9, in req\nAssertionError: {'judgement_id': 1592, 'view_id': 'v9', 'seq': 1884, 'input_id': 'day:2026-09-20', 'rung': 2, 'reasons': \"The market reference is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which is rung 2. The evidence-based estimate is now around $410 billion: NVIDIA reported $164 billion in the first half, Q3 total-revenue guidance and the recent Data Center mix imply roughly $100 billion for Q3, and a roughly $146 billion Q4 is supported by the expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp. SemiAnalysis's forecast of second-half Data Center revenue 20% above analyst estimates is a meaningful upside input: applying it to the roughly $250 billion of second-half revenue implied by the $414 billion reference would point to about $464 billion for the year. I discount that forecast because it does not state its underlying estimate and its implied Q4 is much higher than the company has quantified; the resulting central estimate remains near $410 billion. That crosses the $400 billion boundary into rung 2, but not the $450 billion boundary. Supply and competition risks, and NVIDIA's exclusion of China compute revenue from its outlook, temper the upside.\", 'cited_evidence_json': '[\"e74\", \"e2517\", \"e2574\", \"e4995\", \"e2848\", \"e3219\", \"e2567\", \"e3222\", \"e4765\", \"e976\", \"e2510\", \"e4556\", \"e4557\", \"e2562\", \"e2572\", \"e109\", \"e153\", \"e4894\", \"e4996\"]', 'cited_views_json': '[]', 'pushes_json': '[{\"evidence_id\": \"e74\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2517\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2574\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e4995\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2848\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e3219\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2567\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e3222\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e4765\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e976\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2510\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e4556\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e4557\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2562\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2572\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e109\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e153\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e4894\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e4996\", \"push\": \"none\"}]', 'changed': 1, 'why_changed': \"The rung moves from 3 to 2 because the quantified SemiAnalysis forecast for second-half revenue above analyst estimates lifts the implied FY2027 outcome across $400 billion, while the Q3 guide and first-half reported revenue anchor the estimate. The updated China-authorization theme adds some upside possibility, but NVIDIA's stated no-China-revenue outlook prevents treating that as booked revenue.\", 'config_checksum': '4f2aad7d25dae54d', 'call_id': 8737, 'request_sha256': '958bb92ef74038b0cd4e7038bf5b85cb5cc141c502e826df62ee6f4af1b8dbe6', 'publication_day': '2026-09-20', 'theme_pushes_json': '[{\"view_id\": \"v10\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v25\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v26\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v5\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}]', 'reference': 'The market reference supplied by the previous conclusion is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion).', 'implied_outcome': \"Approximately $410 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and roughly $146 billion estimated for Q4. The Q4 estimate reflects management's expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp, with a discounted contribution from SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half Data Center revenue would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\"}\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
