o aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance is supplied, so there is no external reference figure to place on the ladder. The carried base case of roughly $10–11 billion is in rung 4.'), ('v8', '2026-08-02', 2694, 'Analyst consensus is the reference; no numeric consensus is supplied in the current evidence. The carried comparison places it below the implied outcome, most consistently on rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-03', 2728, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support obligations is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is the available reference and sits in rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio proposal is not itself an established reference for committed obligations.'), ('v1', '2026-08-05', 2808, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support commitments is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio guarantee headline, if fully committed, would be in rung 5, but is not the most reliable reference for the committed amount by the due date.'), ('v8', '2026-08-05', 2805, 'Analyst consensus; no numeric figure is supplied in this view. The carried comparison places the reference most consistently in rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-06', 2871, 'No explicit market consensus or aggregate NVIDIA guidance is supplied. The carried non-Ohio estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the carried estimate including a discounted Ohio contribution is about $20–21 billion, rung 5. The reported $250 billion Ohio figure, if taken in full, would also be rung 5 but is not the reference forecast used here.'), ('v8', '2026-08-09', 2975, 'Analyst consensus, as described in the previous conclusion, is $350bn to below $400bn: rung 2. No exact consensus estimate is supplied.'), ('v8', '2026-08-25', 4589, \"The carried-forward analyst-consensus reference is $350 billion to below $400 billion, 