billion, also rung 2. FY2027 revenue of approximately $418.9 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 plus $96.2 billion Q2, an estimated $113.6 billion Q3 (3.1% above the $110.16 billion high end of gu\n2026-09-16 v14 8204 127 False False Wall Street analyst expectations of about $411 billion (e4097, e4348) are in rung 2; Zacks' 87.4% growth estimate implies about $404.5 billion using FY2026 revenue, also rung 2. About $419 billion: reported Q1 and Q2 revenue total $177.8 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $113.6 billion by applying the reported 3.1% average beat to the $110.1\n2026-09-17 v14 8312 123 False False Wall Street analysts expect about $411 billion for FY2027 (rung 2); Zacks’ 87.4% growth estimate implies about $404.5 billion using FY2026 revenue of approximately $215.9 billion (also rung 2). Using Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, estimate Q3 at about $113.6 billion by applying the reported 3.1% average beat to the $110.16 bill\n2026-09-18 v14 8508 139 False False The latest supplied direct analyst expectation is $411 billion for FY2027, which is rung 2. Zacks' 87.4% growth estimate applied to FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies roughly $404.5 billion, also rung 2. About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 reported revenue total $177.8 billion; the $108 billion Q3 guide, adjusted toward the $113–114 billion analyst estimate and the recent \n2026-09-19 v14 8620 131 False False Wall Street analysts expect about $411 billion of FY2027 revenue, placing the reference at rung 2. Zacks' estimate of 87.4% growth applied to FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies about $405 billion, also rung 2. Approximately $418 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2, about $113.5 billion estimated for Q3, and about $127 billion for Q4 by carrying r\n2026-09-20 v14 8729 119 False False Market expectation is about $411 billion for FY2027, rung 2 ($400 billion to less than $450 billion). Zacks' 87.4% growth estimate applied to FY2026 reve