ompany-based reference is $43 billion: $25 billion of equity investment commitments reported as of July 26 plus $18 billion earmarked for the rest of FY2027. That reference sits in rung 3. Th\n09-15 8452 he company-based reference is $43 billion: $25 billion of equity investment commitments reported as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027. That reference sits in rung 3. Th\n09-16 8630 About $43 billion, with some possibility of modest additional commitments: the disclosed $25 billion plus the $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027. I do not count the mo\n09-17 8746 About $43 billion, derived from the $25 billion reported commitment balance plus the $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027. The reported and estimated amounts already inv\n09-18 8965 About $43 billion, derived from the $25 billion reported commitment balance plus the $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027. The evidence does not establish a quantified additi\n09-19 9074 The evidence implies roughly $43 billion or less as the most defensible commitment envelope at the FY2027 filing: the $25 billion reported balance plus the $18 billion remainder commitment. That \n09-20 9175 $40–45 billion, centered near $43 billion: carry forward the reported $25 billion commitment balance together with the stated $18 billion remainder-of-FY2027 commitment, without adding later deal\nTIGHT 25\nDRAW 3 v41\n5978 2026-08-30 More than $40 billion of FY2028 CPU revenue, derived by more than doubling the stated $20 billion FY2027 expectation. That supports rung 2, but the evidence does not establish a level of at least $50 billion.\n6213 2026-08-31 More than $40 billion of CPU revenue in FY2028, derived by more than doubling the $20 billion FY2027 expectation. No Vera-only amount is supplied, and the evidence does not quantify the outcome at $50 billion or more.\n6435 2026-09-01 The guidance implies FY2028 CPU revenue above $40 billion, but does not state a precise figure or quantify Vera’s share separately. With no new evidence to move the Vera-specific forecast across the $50 billion boundary, the implied outcome remains rung 2.\n6661 2026-09-03 The best forecast remains rung 2 ($40 billion to less than $50 billion), using the FY2028 CPU-revenue outlook as the available proxy; the evidence does not quantify Vera's share or support a more precise Vera-only figure.\n6856 2026-09-04 The outlook implies total FY2028 CPU revenue above $40 billion ($20 billion in FY2027, more than doubled), but gives no figure for Vera’s share. No Vera-specific amount can be derived, so the existing forecast remains rung 2.\n6964 2026-09-05 The evidence implies FY2028 total CPU revenue above $40 billion, but gives no Vera-specific revenue figure or share. Accordingly, the carried forecast remains rung 2, using the broad-CPU outlook as a proxy rather than treating it as a Vera-specific result.\n7153 2026-09-06 No Vera-specific figure is supplied. Using the total CPU outlook of more than $40 billion as the proxy, as before, implies rung 2; the evidence does not establish Vera's share of that total.\n7284 2026-09-07 The stated expectation implies more than $40 billion of total CPU revenue in FY2028. Applying that aggregate as a proxy leaves Vera near the $40 billion rung-2 boundary, but the evidence provides no Vera-specific allocation.\n7382 2026-09-08 The supplied expectation implies total FY2028 CPU revenue above $40 billion. Because the evidence does not state what share is Vera, it does not establish a Vera-specific figure; the existing roughly $40 billion proxy remains the forecast basis.\n7502 2026-09-09 The stated FY2027 total CPU expectation is $20 billion, and NVIDIA expects FY2028 total CPU revenue to more than double it, implying over $40 billion for CPUs overall. No Vera share is stated, so the evidence supports only the prior roughly $40 billion total-CPU proxy for Vera, not a separately derived Vera revenue figure.\n7740 2026-09-10 The $20 billion FY2027 total-CPU anchor doubled gives a roughly $40 billion gross proxy, while the direct Vera statement specifies doubling but not Vera's baseline. Discounting for Vera's unestablished share of total CPU revenue and unproven shipment volume implies a central FY2028 Vera estimate in the mid-$30 billions.\n7893 2026-09-11 The evidence implies a mid-$30-billion Vera FY2028 outcome, carried from the prior estimate: the broader CPU outlook points above $40 billion, while Vera is said to double from an unquantified FY2027 base and its share of total CPU revenue is not stated. That estimate remains below the $40 billion rung-2 threshold.\n8037 2026-09-12 Roughly the high-$30 billions for FY2028: discount the stated more-than-$40-billion target because the evidence does not show Vera shipment volume in hand, while giving weight to the stated broad deployment footprint and the expanding server-CPU market.\n8134 2026-09-13 High-$30 billions (roughly $38–39 billion): the more-than-$40-billion management target is discounted because the evidence does not show Vera shipment volume in hand. That estimate remains below the $40 billion rung-2 boundary.\n8297 2026-09-14 Discount the greater-than-$40-billion management target because the evidence does not show Vera shipment volume in hand. The implied outcome remains in the high-$30 billions, below $40 billion and within rung 3.\n8433 2026-09-15 Approximately the high-$30 billions (around $38 billion): the more-than-$40-billion management target is discounted because the evidence does not show Vera shipment volume in hand. The implied figure remains below the $40 billion rung boundary.\n8616 2026-09-16 The management forecast implies more than $40 billion from a $20 billion FY2027 base. Discounting that target because the evidence does not show Vera shipment volume in hand, while crediting the broad deployment expectations, implies roughly $38–40 billion for FY2028.\n8753 2026-09-17 About $38–40 billion: discount the more-than-$40-billion management target for the still-unshipped product and lack of quantified volume in hand. This remains below the $40 billion rung-2 boundary.\n8953 2026-09-18 The management target implies more than $40 billion, but discounted for execution and the absence of Vera shipment volume in hand, the implied outcome remains around $38–40 billion. That is below the $40 billion threshold for rung 2 and within rung 3.\n9071 2026-09-19 Roughly $38–39 billion for FY2028: the management reference implies more than $40 billion, but I discount it for the lack of Vera volume in hand and the new competitive-performance evidence. Broad deployment expectations and CPU-market growth provide some offset, without establishing NVIDIA’s share.\n9166 2026-09-20 Roughly $38–39 billion for FY2028: the stated more-than-double expectation points above $40 billion, but is discounted for a forward Vera target without shipment volume in hand, with the competitive evidence adding execution risk.\nTIGHT 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\nD=decimal.Decimal\ndef db(i,name='\\\\''views'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef req(a,j):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n assert c and c['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\'']==j['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''] and c['\\\\''purpose'\\\\'']=='\\\\''judge'\\\\'',dict(j)\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\''])\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\''\"'^- (e'\"\\\\d+) \\\\[.*?(?=\"'^- e'\"\\\\d+ \\\\[|\\\\Z)'\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\ndef evidence(t):\n b=t.split('\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0]\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\n return m\ndef user(d):\n return next(m['\\\\''content'\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\''messages'\\\\''] if m['\\\\''role'\\\\'']=='\\\\''user'\\\\'')\nUNIT=r'\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\''\nNUM=r'\\\\''\\\\d+(?:,\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?'\\\\''\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\''(?<\"'!['\"\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\"'$?'\"\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\s*\\\\\"'$?'\"\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\"'\\\\'',re.I)\nMULT={'\\\\''trillion'\\\\'':1000,'\\\\''trillions'\\\\'':1000,'\\\\''t'\\\\'':1000,'\\\\''billion'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''billions'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''bn'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''b'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''million'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\''),'\\\\''millions'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\''),'\\\\''mm'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\''),'\\\\''m'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\'')}\ndef figures(t,unit):\n out=[]\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\'''\\\\''):\n  u=m['\\\\''unit'\\\\''].lower()\n  if (u in MULT)\"'!=(unit=='\"'\\\\''USD'\\\\''):continue\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\n  if m['\\\\''sign'\\\\''] in ('\\\\''-'\\\\'','\\\\''−'\\\\''):mult=-mult\n  for g in ('\\\\''lo'\\\\'','\\\\''hi'\\\\''):\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\'','\\\\'','\\\\'''\\\\''))*mult)\n return out\ndef snippets(ed):\n return [re.split(r'\\\\''\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\''] '\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\ndef prior_text(t):\n return t.split('\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\''] '\\\\'',1)[1]\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\'''\\\\'',re.I))\ndef record(i):\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\''USD'\\\\'','\\\\''percent'\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\"))\nfor i,id in [(1,'\\\\''v4'\\\\''),(2,'\\\\''v14'\\\\''),(3,'\\\\''v3'\\\\'')]:\n v,a,_=record(i)\n j=v.execute(\\\"select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day='\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\''\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n print(i,id,'\\\\''creation'\\\\'',tuple(v.execute(\\\"select created_seq,created_from_input,question from views where view_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()))\n print('\\\\''band'\\\\'',list(map(tuple,v.execute('\\\\''select position,lo,hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position'\\\\'',(id,)))))\n if i==3:\n  d,raw=req(a,j); ed=evidence(user(d))\n  for k in ('\\\\''e60'\\\\'','\\\\''e5088'\\\\'','\\\\''e2715'\\\\'','\\\\''e4190'\\\\''):print(ed[k][:550])\nv,a,_=record(2)\nfor call in (1736,4485,8011):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call,)).fetchone()\n data=json.loads(c['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\n for e in data['\\\\''evidence'\\\\'']:\n  if '\\\\''exceed analyst estimates by 20%'\\\\'' in e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''] or '\\\\''equity investment commitments of \"'$25 billion'\"'\\\\'' in e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''] or '\\\\''averaged 3.1% above'\\\\'' in e['\\\\''quote'\\\\'']:\n   assert e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''] in user(json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\'']))\n   print('\\\\''source in raw extraction'\\\\'',call,e['\\\\''id'\\\\''],e['\\\\''links'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\nD=decimal.Decimal\ndef db(i,name='\\\\''views'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef req(a,j):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n assert c and c['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\'']==j['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''] and c['\\\\''purpose'\\\\'']=='\\\\''judge'\\\\'',dict(j)\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\''])\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\''\"'^- (e'\"\\\\d+) \\\\[.*?(?=\"'^- e'\"\\\\d+ \\\\[|\\\\Z)'\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\ndef evidence(t):\n b=t.split('\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0]\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\n return m\ndef user(d):\n return next(m['\\\\''content'\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\''messages'\\\\''] if m['\\\\''role'\\\\'']=='\\\\''user'\\\\'')\nUNIT=r'\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\''\nNUM=r'\\\\''\\\\d+(?:,\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?'\\\\''\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\''(?<\"'!['\"\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\"'$?'\"\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\s*\\\\\"'$?'\"\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\"'\\\\'',re.I)\nMULT={'\\\\''trillion'\\\\'':1000,'\\\\''trillions'\\\\'':1000,'\\\\''t'\\\\'':1000,'\\\\''billion'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''billions'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''bn'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''b'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''million'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\''),'\\\\''millions'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\''),'\\\\''mm'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\''),'\\\\''m'\\\\'':D('\\\\''.001'\\\\'')}\ndef figures(t,unit):\n out=[]\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\'''\\\\''):\n  u=m['\\\\''unit'\\\\''].lower()\n  if (u in MULT)\"'!=(unit=='\"'\\\\''USD'\\\\''):continue\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\n  if m['\\\\''sign'\\\\''] in ('\\\\''-'\\\\'','\\\\''−'\\\\''):mult=-mult\n  for g in ('\\\\''lo'\\\\'','\\\\''hi'\\\\''):\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\'','\\\\'','\\\\'''\\\\''))*mult)\n return out\ndef snippets(ed):\n return [re.split(r'\\\\''\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\''] '\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\ndef prior_text(t):\n return t.split('\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\''] '\\\\'',1)[1]\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\'''\\\\'',re.I))\ndef record(i):\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\''archive'\\\\'')\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\''USD'\\\\'','\\\\''percent'\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\"))\nfor i,id in [(1,'\\\\''v4'\\\\''),(2,'\\\\''v14'\\\\''),(3,'\\\\''v3'\\\\'')]:\n v,a,_=record(i)\n j=v.execute(\\\"select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day='\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\''\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n print(i,id,'\\\\''creation'\\\\'',tuple(v.execute(\\\"select created_seq,created_from_input,question from views where view_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()))\n print('\\\\''band'\\\\'',list(map(tuple,v.execute('\\\\''select position,lo,hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position'\\\\'',(id,)))))\n if i==3:\n  d,raw=req(a,j); ed=evidence(user(d))\n  for k in ('\\\\''e60'\\\\'','\\\\''e5088'\\\\'','\\\\''e2715'\\\\'','\\\\''e4190'\\\\''):print(ed[k][:550])\nv,a,_=record(2)\nfor call in (1736,4485,8011):\n c=a.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call,)).fetchone()\n data=json.loads(c['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\n for e in data['\\\\''evidence'\\\\'']:\n  if '\\\\''exceed analyst estimates by 20%'\\\\'' in e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''] or '\\\\''equity investment commitments of \"'$25 billion'\"'\\\\'' in e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''] or '\\\\''averaged 3.1% above'\\\\'' in e['\\\\''quote'\\\\'']:\n   assert e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''] in user(json.loads(c['\\\\''request_json'\\\\'']))\n   print('\\\\''source in raw extraction'\\\\'',call,e['\\\\''id'\\\\''],e['\\\\''links'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"1 v4 creation (22, 'gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b', \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\")\nband [(1, 431200000000.0, None), (2, 392000000000.0, 431200000000.0), (3, 352800000000.0, 392000000000.0), (4, 313600000000.0, 352800000000.0), (5, None, 313600000000.0)]\n2 v14 creation (148, 'gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4', 'How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?')\nband [(1, 450000000000.0, None), (2, 400000000000.0, 450000000000.0), (3, 350000000000.0, 400000000000.0), (4, 300000000000.0, 350000000000.0), (5, None, 300000000000.0)]\n3 v3 creation (22, 'gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b', 'What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?')\nband [(1, 431200000000.0, None), (2, 392000000000.0, 431200000000.0), (3, 352800000000.0, 392000000000.0), (4, 313600000000.0, 352800000000.0), (5, None, 313600000000.0)]\n- e60 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected NVIDIA data-center compute revenue for the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e140, e1116; the argument counts one claim, one more ou\n- e5088 [third_party_view; Manali Pradhan, CFA; original source Manali Pradhan, CFA 2026-09-15; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] Manali Pradhan estimated NVIDIA could report fiscal Q3 2027 revenue of about $113 billion to $114 billion.\n    Quote: However, I think Nvidia could report third-quarter revenue of around $113 billion to $114 billion.\n- e2715 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 total revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.\n    Quote: Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2740, e2792, e3454; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e4190 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:89698c9955cf8aa35b642970 2026-09-04] NVIDIA's FY2027 Q3 guidance implied 12% sequential total revenue growth at the midpoint.\n    Quote: In the meantime, Nvidia's fiscal 2027 third-quarter guidance implies 12% sequential growth at the midpoint.\nsource in raw extraction 1736 e5 ['v9']\nsource in raw extraction 4485 e14 ['v29']\nsource in raw extraction 8011 e3 ['v14']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
